Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Swap Clients icon for a plain profile glyph, simplify
 workspace pill
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The DiceBear identicon on the Clients button read as a random colorful
blob rather than an icon — replaced with a plain Users glyph (same
treatment as every other rail icon) so it just looks like a normal nav
button.

The active-client quick-link pill drops its text label (redundant with
the title tooltip and the dropdown row) and sizes its square initials
avatar up, so it reads as a standalone icon-button instead of a cramped
icon+caption pill.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011PX9qLTKPtXba6ncjAwLyN
